WEBVTT

00:05:29.828 --> 00:05:31.920
they learn things
in three to five trials --

00:05:31.944 --> 00:05:33.099
it's a good brain.

00:05:33.123 --> 00:05:36.004
And the spatial memory is unusually good.

00:05:36.028 --> 00:05:39.660
They will even end their forage
and make a beeline

00:05:39.684 --> 00:05:41.245
all the way back to their den.

00:05:41.269 --> 00:05:43.559
The divers watching them
are completely lost,

00:05:43.583 --> 00:05:44.743
but they can get back,

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:48.329
so it's really quite refined
memory capability.

00:05:48.353 --> 00:05:49.988
Now, in terms of cognitive skills,

00:05:50.012 --> 00:05:52.863
look at this sleeping behavior
in the cuttlefish.

00:05:52.887 --> 00:05:55.269
Especially on the right,
you see the eye twitching.

00:05:55.293 --> 00:05:58.455
This is rapid eye movement
kind of dreaming

00:05:58.479 --> 00:06:00.651
that we only thought
mammals and birds did.